    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0676" n="576" xml:id="pg576"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">251.11 Insull, Samuel/372: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fish</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-18T18:00:00+02:00">March 18, 1934—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 18—3:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. Legation assumes Athens has advised Department of Insull’s recent movement. I
                    am orally but officially informed that the Egyptian Government will not permit
                    him to land anywhere in Egypt.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fish</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
